// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/tri/t27b/i128_plan.t27 -- how t27b holds a run-time i128 (issues #8736, #8763 and #8913, the three stages
; that #7915 tracks; t27b coverage epic #6063, written in t27 under the port epic #6198).
; --
; The design the owner chose on 2026-10-10 (option A of the design comment on #7915): an i128 is a type of
; t27b's code generator in its own right, held in a pair of X registers, the low word in the first one, as
; AAPCS64 holds it. A result comes back in x0 (low) and x1 (high); an argument takes the next even-numbered
; pair, x0:x1 up to x6:x7, and the stack after that; in memory it is 16 bytes, aligned to 16, the low word
; first (Zig 0.16: `@sizeOf(i128)` and `@alignOf(i128)` are both 16, measured on the t27c lab for #7915).
; Every decision about the pair is in this file and reaches cli/t27b through `t27c gen-rust`
; (gen/rust/tri/t27b/i128_plan.rs, mounted by cli/t27b/src/ir.rs): which type text is an i128, where a
; variable's pair lives, how a literal splits into its two words, which instructions compare two pairs and
; which compute `+ - *` and `@divTrunc` on them. The glue in cli/t27b/src/codegen.rs moves the words and emits
; the steps, and refuses as REFUSED every i128 shape this file does not cover yet, so nothing outside it is
; compiled to a guess.
; --
; Stage 1 is what specs/port/bootstrap/src/phi_f64_literals.t27 needs (the conformance spec is
; specs/tri/t27b/conformance/i128_return.t27):
;   - NAME is read as a fn's result type. A parameter, a struct field, an optional and an array of i128 keep
;     their `type i128` refusal.
;   - a variable lives in HOME_WORDS words of its frame, the low word first; those homes are laid out before
;     any other variable, so each is 16-byte aligned.
;   - a literal is split into its two words (`lit_lo`, `lit_hi`): the two's complement of its sign and
;     magnitude. Each word is then put in a register as any 64-bit constant is (a64.t27's mov_imm).
;   - every comparison is two instructions on the two words (`cmp_step`): `cmp` of the low words, then for
;     `==` and `!=` `ccmp` of the high words, which sets CCMP_NZCV (Z clear: unequal) when the low words
;     differ, and for an ordered comparison `sbcs xzr` of the high words, whose N and V are those of the
;     128-bit difference, so LT and GE are exact. `>` and `<=` exchange the operands (`cmp_swaps`) and test LT
;     and GE. The condition is `cmp_cond`. `holds` runs these steps on a model of the flags, and the tests
;     check it against the order of the integers for every pair of SAMPLES values.
; Stage 2 is what specs/tri/t27b/source_text.t27 needs (the conformance spec is
; specs/tri/t27b/conformance/i128_arith.t27; the traps are cli/t27b/tests/i128_traps.t27):
;   - NAME is read as a local's annotation too. A module constant declared NAME is a pair constant where a
;     run-time value is wanted: beside a run-time value, or folded to one value (wide_plan.t27's `run_time`).
;   - a lossless widening (`@intCast` of a narrower integer) is the operand's 64-bit extension and its sign,
;     or 0 for an unsigned operand.
;   - checked `+`, `-`, `*` and `@divTrunc` are programs of steps on the four words of the operands (`step`).
;     The glue copies the words into TEMPS consecutive temps and emits each step's word (`step_word`); a trap
;     step branches to the operator's site, or to the next one (`trap_site`). `+` is adds then adcs, and `-`
;     subs then sbcs, both trapping on the V of the high word (`overflow_cond`). `*` takes the magnitudes,
;     traps unless their product fits 128 bits (two high words not 0, a cross product's high word not 0, a
;     carry out of the high word), forms the product with mul and umulh, gives it the operands' sign, and traps
;     unless that result has the sign it should. `@divTrunc` traps on a zero divisor at its own site and on
;     minInt / -1 at the next, then calls the division routine.
;   - the division routine is written below (`t27b_i128_div`) and spliced into a program that names
;     one of BUILTINS, renamed from PORT to HELPER, t27b's reserved prefix, as libm.t27's routines are: binary
;     long division of the magnitudes, with one division of words when both fit 64 bits and two 32-bit digits
;     per division of words when the divisor fits 32 bits. Every name in it starts with `t27b_`, so none
;     shadows a name of the program it joins.
;   - `run_steps` runs a program on a model of the twelve step registers and NZCV, and a test checks it
;     against exact i128 arithmetic (Zig's own under `t27c test-report`) for every pair of SAMPLES values.
; Stage 3 is what specs/tri/t27b/eval_arith.t27 needs (the conformance spec is
; specs/tri/t27b/conformance/i128_ops.t27; the new traps are in cli/t27b/tests/i128_traps.t27 too):
;   - NAME is read as a parameter's type and a struct field's. A parameter takes the next even-numbered pair of
;     argument registers (`arg_reg`, `arg_next`: AAPCS64 C.10 to C.13); the callee stores the pair in its home
;     with one stp. A pair that would go on the stack is refused.
;   - a struct field of type NAME is BYTES bytes, aligned to ALIGN (builtin_plan.t27's `abi_bytes`); its two
;     words are loaded with one ldp and stored with one stp (`pair_word`) while the offset is in their reach
;     (`pair_imm`), and refused past it.
;   - `+%`, `-%` and `*%` are programs without a trap; `&`, `|` and `^` act word by word.
;   - `@rem` traps on a zero divisor, as `@divTrunc` does, then calls the remainder routine
;     (`t27b_i128_rem`, the division routine's remainder): minInt % -1 is 0, as Zig's Debug build leaves it.
;   - `<<` and `>>` take the amount's word (a u32 extended to 64 bits). A checked shift traps unless the
;     amount is below 128, where Zig's `<< @intCast(n)` panics; then both the shift below 64 and the shift from
;     64 up are formed and bit 6 of the amount picks one with csel. `<<` drops the bits shifted out; `>>` is
;     arithmetic. A wrapping shift reads only the amount's low seven bits.
;   - a checked cast of an i128 to a narrower integer type (`amt as u32`) traps unless the high word is the low
;     word's extension (`cast_program`); the glue then checks the low word as a cast from u64 or i64.
; --
; The oracle: AAPCS64 (section 6.8.2, rules C.10 to C.13: a 16-byte integer argument), Zig 0.16's layout and
; Debug traps (measured on the t27c lab for #7915), and the Arm ARM's ADDS, ADCS, SUBS, SBCS, CCMP, MUL and
; UMULH; the instruction words are a64.t27's, checked there against GNU as, and some step words here too.
; The tests' order of two integers is computed from their signs and magnitudes, apart from the flags, and
; their sums, differences, products, quotients, remainders, bitwise results and shifts are the reference's i128
; arithmetic. `overflow_cond` was the hand-written `overflow_cond` of cli/t27b/src/codegen.rs (#8763 ports it).
; No unary operator (#6549), no wrapping operator and no char literal (#7604) below.
; ASCII only (L3)
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

module T27bI128Plan;

use tri::t27b::a64;

/// The type text t27b reads as a run-time i128 (a fn's result type, a local's annotation, a module constant's).
pub const NAME : str = "i128";
/// What an i128 shape t27b does not lower yet is refused as: the construct the refusal had before this plan.
pub const REFUSED : str = "type i128";

/// AAPCS64 returns an i128 in x0 (the low word) and x1 (the high word).
pub const RET_LO : u8 = 0;
pub const RET_HI : u8 = 1;
/// In memory the low word comes first (little-endian): the high word is HI_OFF bytes after it.
pub const HI_OFF : u32 = 8;
/// A variable's home: this many 8-byte words of the frame, BYTES in all, aligned to ALIGN.
pub const HOME_WORDS : u32 = 2;
pub const BYTES : u32 = 16;
pub const ALIGN : u32 = 16;
/// x0 to x7 carry integer arguments.
pub const ARG_REGS : u32 = 8;

const MAX64 : u64 = t27b_i128_max64;
const SIGN64 : u64 = t27b_i128_sign64;
const LOW32 : u64 = t27b_i128_low32;

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- arguments

/// AAPCS64 C.10: an argument aligned to 16 starts at an even-numbered register, so the next general register
/// number `ngrn` is rounded up to even.
pub fn pair_first(ngrn: u32) -> u32 {
    return ngrn + (ngrn & 1);
}

/// AAPCS64 C.11 and C.13: the pair is passed in registers when it starts at x6 at the latest; otherwise it goes
/// on the stack, 16-byte aligned, and no later integer argument takes a register.
pub fn pair_in_regs(ngrn: u32) -> bool {
    return pair_first(ngrn) + 2 <= ARG_REGS;
}

/// The register an integer argument starts at, from the next general register number `ngrn`: ngrn itself, or
/// for a pair `pair_first`. A pair that does not fit goes on the stack, as an argument past x7 does: its number
/// is then ARG_REGS or more, which cli/t27b's Program::stack_args reads as a stack word.
pub fn arg_reg(ngrn: u32, pair: bool) -> u32 {
    if (pair == false) { return ngrn; }
    if (pair_in_regs(ngrn)) { return pair_first(ngrn); }
    if (ngrn < ARG_REGS) { return ARG_REGS; }
    return ngrn;
}

/// The next general register number after an argument that starts at register k: two on for a pair in
/// registers, one on otherwise, so no integer argument after a pair on the stack takes a register (C.13).
pub fn arg_next(k: u32, pair: bool) -> u32 {
    if (pair and k < ARG_REGS) { return k + 2; }
    return k + 1;
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- memory

/// Can one ldp or stp reach an i128 `off` bytes from its base? Their signed offset is a multiple of 8, at most
/// 504. cli/t27b refuses a pair it cannot reach so (a field that far into a struct, a home past the 32nd pair).
pub fn pair_imm(off: u32) -> bool {
    return off <= 504 and off % 8 == 0;
}

/// The word that loads (`ldp lo, hi, [base, #off]`) or stores (`stp`) the two words of an i128 in memory, the low
/// word first: a struct field, a parameter's home.
pub fn pair_word(load: bool, lo: u8, hi: u8, base: u8, off: u32) -> u32 {
    if (load) { return ldp_x(lo, hi, base, off as i32); }
    return stp_x(lo, hi, base, off as i32);
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- literals

/// The low word of the literal whose sign is `neg` and whose magnitude's low word is `mag_lo`.
pub fn lit_lo(neg: bool, mag_lo: u64) -> u64 {
    if (neg) { return t27b_i128_neg(mag_lo, 0, 0); }
    return mag_lo;
}

/// The high word of that literal, whose magnitude's high word is `mag_hi`: the high word itself, or for a
/// negative literal the high word of the magnitude's two's complement.
pub fn lit_hi(neg: bool, mag_lo: u64, mag_hi: u64) -> u64 {
    if (neg == false) { return mag_hi; }
    return t27b_i128_neg(mag_lo, mag_hi, 1);
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- comparisons

/// The comparisons, by their CmpOp number (cli/t27b/src/ir.rs, specs/tri/t27b/cmp_op.t27).
pub const EQ : u8 = 0;
pub const NE : u8 = 1;
pub const LT : u8 = 2;
pub const LE : u8 = 3;
pub const GT : u8 = 4;
pub const GE : u8 = 5;

/// One step of a comparison of the pairs x and y, on word k of each: `cmp xk, yk`; `ccmp xk, yk, #CCMP_NZCV, eq`;
/// `sbcs xzr, xk, yk`.
pub const STEP_CMP : u8 = 0;
pub const STEP_CCMP : u8 = 1;
pub const STEP_SBCS : u8 = 2;
/// The flags ccmp sets when the low words differ: all clear, so EQ fails and NE holds.
pub const CCMP_NZCV : u32 = 0;
/// The conditions the steps test, in a64.t27's 4-bit encoding.
pub const COND_EQ : u32 = 0;
pub const COND_NE : u32 = 1;
pub const COND_HS : u32 = 2;
pub const COND_LO : u32 = 3;
pub const COND_MI : u32 = 4;
pub const COND_VS : u32 = 6;
pub const COND_GE : u32 = 10;
pub const COND_LT : u32 = 11;

/// Step k of comparison `op`: word 0 (the low words) first, then word 1 (the high words).
pub fn cmp_step(op: u8, k: u32) -> u8 {
    if (k == 0) { return STEP_CMP; }
    if (op == EQ or op == NE) { return STEP_CCMP; }
    return STEP_SBCS;
}

/// `x > y` is `y < x` and `x <= y` is `y >= x`: these two compare the operands exchanged.
pub fn cmp_swaps(op: u8) -> bool {
    return op == GT or op == LE;
}

/// The condition that holds after the two steps exactly when `x op y`.
pub fn cmp_cond(op: u8) -> u32 {
    if (op == EQ) { return COND_EQ; }
    if (op == NE) { return COND_NE; }
    if (op == LT or op == GT) { return COND_LT; }
    return COND_GE;
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- overflow

/// The condition a checked `+` or `-` traps on after adds or subs (after adcs or sbcs of an i128's high words):
/// VS for a signed type, LO (a borrow) for an unsigned difference, HS (a carry) for an unsigned sum.
pub fn overflow_cond(signed: bool, sub: bool) -> u32 {
    if (signed) { return COND_VS; }
    if (sub) { return COND_LO; }
    return COND_HS;
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- arithmetic: the programs

/// The operators with a program, by their ArithOp number (cli/t27b/src/ir.rs; eval_arith.t27's OP_ codes).
const OP_ADD : u8 = 0;
const OP_SUB : u8 = 1;
const OP_MUL : u8 = 2;
const OP_ADD_W : u8 = 3;
const OP_SUB_W : u8 = 4;
const OP_MUL_W : u8 = 5;
const OP_DIV : u8 = 6;
const OP_DIV_W : u8 = 7;
const OP_REM : u8 = 8;
const OP_AND : u8 = 9;
const OP_OR : u8 = 10;
const OP_XOR : u8 = 11;
const OP_SHL : u8 = 12;
const OP_SHR : u8 = 13;
const OP_SHL_W : u8 = 14;
const OP_SHR_W : u8 = 15;

/// A program: the steps of one operator on two pairs. A shift's second pair is its amount, extended to 128
/// bits; a cast's is 0.
pub const PROG_NONE : u8 = 0;
pub const PROG_ADD : u8 = 1;
pub const PROG_SUB : u8 = 2;
pub const PROG_MUL : u8 = 3;
pub const PROG_DIV : u8 = 4;
pub const PROG_ADD_W : u8 = 5;
pub const PROG_SUB_W : u8 = 6;
pub const PROG_MUL_W : u8 = 7;
pub const PROG_REM : u8 = 8;
pub const PROG_AND : u8 = 9;
pub const PROG_OR : u8 = 10;
pub const PROG_XOR : u8 = 11;
pub const PROG_SHL : u8 = 12;
pub const PROG_SHR : u8 = 13;
pub const PROG_SHL_W : u8 = 14;
pub const PROG_SHR_W : u8 = 15;
pub const PROG_CAST_U : u8 = 16;
pub const PROG_CAST_S : u8 = 17;
pub const PROG_TRUNC : u8 = 18;
/// The last program, for the tests.
const PROG_LAST : u8 = 18;

/// The program of ArithOp `op` on two i128s; PROG_NONE for the wrapping division, which only the wrap mode of
/// the differential test makes.
pub fn program(op: u8) -> u8 {
    if (op == OP_ADD) { return PROG_ADD; }
    if (op == OP_SUB) { return PROG_SUB; }
    if (op == OP_MUL) { return PROG_MUL; }
    if (op == OP_DIV) { return PROG_DIV; }
    if (op == OP_ADD_W) { return PROG_ADD_W; }
    if (op == OP_SUB_W) { return PROG_SUB_W; }
    if (op == OP_MUL_W) { return PROG_MUL_W; }
    if (op == OP_REM) { return PROG_REM; }
    if (op == OP_AND) { return PROG_AND; }
    if (op == OP_OR) { return PROG_OR; }
    if (op == OP_XOR) { return PROG_XOR; }
    if (op == OP_SHL) { return PROG_SHL; }
    if (op == OP_SHR) { return PROG_SHR; }
    if (op == OP_SHL_W) { return PROG_SHL_W; }
    if (op == OP_SHR_W) { return PROG_SHR_W; }
    return PROG_NONE;
}

/// The program of a cast of an i128 to a narrower integer type: a checked cast (`x as u32`) traps unless the
/// high word is the low word's extension, 0 for an unsigned type and the low word's sign for a signed one; the
/// glue then checks the low word as a cast from u64 or i64. A truncating cast has no steps.
pub fn cast_program(signed: bool, checked: bool) -> u8 {
    if (checked == false) { return PROG_TRUNC; }
    if (signed) { return PROG_CAST_S; }
    return PROG_CAST_U;
}

/// Does the program call a routine? A fn that runs one needs a frame, as a fn with a call does.
pub fn calls(prog: u8) -> bool {
    return prog == PROG_DIV or prog == PROG_REM;
}

/// The routine the I_CALL step of program `prog` calls, by its spliced name; empty for a program without one.
pub fn routine(prog: u8) -> str {
    if (prog == PROG_DIV) { return DIV_ROUTINE; }
    if (prog == PROG_REM) { return REM_ROUTINE; }
    return "";
}

/// The registers a step names. R_A0, R_A1, R_B0 and R_B1 are the words of the operands a and b, the low word
/// first, which the glue copies into TEMPS consecutive temps; a program leaves its result in R_A0 (low) and
/// R_A1 (high). R_S0, R_S1 and R_S2 are the scratch registers x8, x16 and x17; R_ZR is the zero register; R_X0
/// to R_X3 are the argument registers x0 to x3 of the call.
pub const R_A0 : u8 = 0;
pub const R_A1 : u8 = 1;
pub const R_B0 : u8 = 2;
pub const R_B1 : u8 = 3;
pub const R_S0 : u8 = 4;
pub const R_S1 : u8 = 5;
pub const R_S2 : u8 = 6;
pub const R_ZR : u8 = 7;
pub const R_X0 : u8 = 8;
pub const R_X1 : u8 = 9;
pub const R_X2 : u8 = 10;
pub const R_X3 : u8 = 11;
/// How many temps a program takes from the glue's temp stack: one per operand word. The result is in the first two.
pub const TEMPS : u32 = 4;

/// The machine register of step register `v`, when the operands' words are in x(first) up.
pub fn reg_of(v: u8, first: u8) -> u8 {
    if (v <= R_B1) { return first + v; }
    if (v == R_S0) { return 8; }
    if (v == R_S1) { return 16; }
    if (v == R_S2) { return 17; }
    if (v == R_ZR) { return 31; }
    return v - R_X0;
}

/// What a step does: one instruction on X registers, destination d, operands n and m, and x the shift amount
/// of I_ASR, I_LSL and I_LSR, imm16 + 65536 * hw of I_MOVZ, nzcv + 16 * cond of I_CCMP, the condition of I_TRAP
/// and I_CSEL (which takes n when it holds, else m). I_TRAP is a branch to the operator's site plus m when the
/// condition holds; I_CALL calls the program's routine. I_LSLV, I_LSRV and I_ASRV shift by m modulo 64.
pub const I_ADDS : u8 = 1;
pub const I_ADCS : u8 = 2;
pub const I_SUBS : u8 = 3;
pub const I_SBCS : u8 = 4;
pub const I_EOR : u8 = 5;
pub const I_ORR : u8 = 6;
pub const I_AND : u8 = 7;
pub const I_ORN : u8 = 8;
pub const I_ASR : u8 = 9;
pub const I_MUL : u8 = 10;
pub const I_UMULH : u8 = 11;
pub const I_MOVZ : u8 = 12;
pub const I_CCMP : u8 = 13;
pub const I_TRAP : u8 = 14;
pub const I_CALL : u8 = 15;
pub const I_LSLV : u8 = 16;
pub const I_LSRV : u8 = 17;
pub const I_ASRV : u8 = 18;
pub const I_LSL : u8 = 19;
pub const I_LSR : u8 = 20;
pub const I_ANDS : u8 = 21;
pub const I_CSEL : u8 = 22;

/// A step, packed into a word: op, then d, n and m a byte each, then x in the high 32 bits.
fn st(op: u8, d: u8, n: u8, m: u8, x: u32) -> u64 {
    return (op as u64) | ((d as u64) << 8) | ((n as u64) << 16) | ((m as u64) << 24) | ((x as u64) << 32);
}

/// Byte k of a packed step: 0 the op, 1 d, 2 n, 3 m.
fn s_part(s: u64, k: u32) -> u8 {
    return ((s >> (8 * k)) & 255) as u8;
}

/// The x of a packed step.
fn s_x(s: u64) -> u32 {
    return (s >> 32) as u32;
}

/// `+`: the low words with adds, the high words with adcs, whose V is the 128-bit sum's overflow.
fn add_step(k: u32) -> u64 {
    if (k == 0) { return st(I_ADDS, R_A0, R_A0, R_B0, 0); }
    if (k == 1) { return st(I_ADCS, R_A1, R_A1, R_B1, 0); }
    return st(I_TRAP, 0, 0, 0, overflow_cond(true, false));
}

/// `-`: the low words with subs, the high words with sbcs.
fn sub_step(k: u32) -> u64 {
    if (k == 0) { return st(I_SUBS, R_A0, R_A0, R_B0, 0); }
    if (k == 1) { return st(I_SBCS, R_A1, R_A1, R_B1, 0); }
    return st(I_TRAP, 0, 0, 0, overflow_cond(true, true));
}

/// `*`, on the magnitudes A of a and B of b and the sign mask s of the result (all ones when it is negative).
fn mul_step(k: u32) -> u64 {
    // A = (a ^ sa) - sa and B = (b ^ sb) - sb, sa and sb the operands' sign masks (asr #63 of the high word).
    if (k == 0) { return st(I_ASR, R_S0, R_A1, 0, 63); }
    if (k == 1) { return st(I_EOR, R_A0, R_A0, R_S0, 0); }
    if (k == 2) { return st(I_EOR, R_A1, R_A1, R_S0, 0); }
    if (k == 3) { return st(I_SUBS, R_A0, R_A0, R_S0, 0); }
    if (k == 4) { return st(I_SBCS, R_A1, R_A1, R_S0, 0); }
    if (k == 5) { return st(I_ASR, R_S1, R_B1, 0, 63); }
    if (k == 6) { return st(I_EOR, R_B0, R_B0, R_S1, 0); }
    if (k == 7) { return st(I_EOR, R_B1, R_B1, R_S1, 0); }
    if (k == 8) { return st(I_SUBS, R_B0, R_B0, R_S1, 0); }
    if (k == 9) { return st(I_SBCS, R_B1, R_B1, R_S1, 0); }
    // s = sa ^ sb, in S0.
    if (k == 10) { return st(I_EOR, R_S0, R_S0, R_S1, 0); }
    // Both high words not 0: A * B is 2^128 or more. ccmp leaves Z set, as if B's were 0, when A's is 0.
    if (k == 11) { return st(I_SUBS, R_ZR, R_A1, R_ZR, 0); }
    if (k == 12) { return st(I_CCMP, 0, R_B1, R_ZR, 4 + 16 * COND_NE); }
    if (k == 13) { return st(I_TRAP, 0, 0, 0, COND_NE); }
    // A cross product's high word not 0: past 2^128 too.
    if (k == 14) { return st(I_UMULH, R_S1, R_A1, R_B0, 0); }
    if (k == 15) { return st(I_UMULH, R_S2, R_A0, R_B1, 0); }
    if (k == 16) { return st(I_ORR, R_S1, R_S1, R_S2, 0); }
    if (k == 17) { return st(I_SUBS, R_ZR, R_S1, R_ZR, 0); }
    if (k == 18) { return st(I_TRAP, 0, 0, 0, COND_NE); }
    // The high word of A * B, in S1: the cross products (one of them is 0) plus the high word of A0 * B0,
    // without a carry out.
    if (k == 19) { return st(I_MUL, R_S1, R_A1, R_B0, 0); }
    if (k == 20) { return st(I_MUL, R_S2, R_A0, R_B1, 0); }
    if (k == 21) { return st(I_ADDS, R_S1, R_S1, R_S2, 0); }
    if (k == 22) { return st(I_UMULH, R_S2, R_A0, R_B0, 0); }
    if (k == 23) { return st(I_ADDS, R_S1, R_S2, R_S1, 0); }
    if (k == 24) { return st(I_TRAP, 0, 0, 0, COND_HS); }
    // The low word, then the result (A * B ^ s) - s in A0:A1.
    if (k == 25) { return st(I_MUL, R_A0, R_A0, R_B0, 0); }
    if (k == 26) { return st(I_EOR, R_A0, R_A0, R_S0, 0); }
    if (k == 27) { return st(I_EOR, R_A1, R_S1, R_S0, 0); }
    if (k == 28) { return st(I_SUBS, R_A0, R_A0, R_S0, 0); }
    if (k == 29) { return st(I_SBCS, R_A1, R_A1, R_S0, 0); }
    // A result that is not 0 and whose sign is not s's did not fit: MI after ccmp of its high word ^ s with 0.
    if (k == 30) { return st(I_ORR, R_S2, R_A0, R_A1, 0); }
    if (k == 31) { return st(I_EOR, R_S1, R_A1, R_S0, 0); }
    if (k == 32) { return st(I_SUBS, R_ZR, R_S2, R_ZR, 0); }
    if (k == 33) { return st(I_CCMP, 0, R_S1, R_ZR, 16 * COND_NE); }
    return st(I_TRAP, 0, 0, 0, COND_MI);
}

/// `@divTrunc`: the two traps Zig's Debug build has, then the routine.
fn div_step(k: u32) -> u64 {
    // A zero divisor: division by zero, at the operator's own site.
    if (k == 0) { return st(I_ORR, R_S0, R_B0, R_B1, 0); }
    if (k == 1) { return st(I_SUBS, R_ZR, R_S0, R_ZR, 0); }
    if (k == 2) { return st(I_TRAP, 0, 0, 0, COND_EQ); }
    // minInt / -1: integer overflow, at the next site. S0 is 0 exactly when b is -1 (both words all ones), S1
    // exactly when a is minInt (the high word 2^63, the low word 0).
    if (k == 3) { return st(I_AND, R_S0, R_B0, R_B1, 0); }
    if (k == 4) { return st(I_ORN, R_S0, R_ZR, R_S0, 0); }
    if (k == 5) { return st(I_MOVZ, R_S1, 0, 0, 32768 + 65536 * 3); }
    if (k == 6) { return st(I_EOR, R_S1, R_A1, R_S1, 0); }
    if (k == 7) { return st(I_ORR, R_S1, R_S1, R_A0, 0); }
    if (k == 8) { return st(I_ORR, R_S0, R_S0, R_S1, 0); }
    if (k == 9) { return st(I_SUBS, R_ZR, R_S0, R_ZR, 0); }
    if (k == 10) { return st(I_TRAP, 0, 0, 1, COND_EQ); }
    // The routine: the four words in x0 to x3, as AAPCS64 passes two i128 arguments; the quotient in x0:x1.
    if (k == 11) { return st(I_ORR, R_X0, R_ZR, R_A0, 0); }
    if (k == 12) { return st(I_ORR, R_X1, R_ZR, R_A1, 0); }
    if (k == 13) { return st(I_ORR, R_X2, R_ZR, R_B0, 0); }
    if (k == 14) { return st(I_ORR, R_X3, R_ZR, R_B1, 0); }
    if (k == 15) { return st(I_CALL, 0, 0, 0, 0); }
    if (k == 16) { return st(I_ORR, R_A0, R_ZR, R_X0, 0); }
    return st(I_ORR, R_A1, R_ZR, R_X1, 0);
}

/// `@rem`: DIV's zero-divisor trap, then the remainder routine, the four words in x0 to x3 and the remainder back
/// in x0:x1 (DIV's steps 11 to 17). minInt % -1 is 0: no second trap.
fn rem_step(k: u32) -> u64 {
    if (k < 3) { return div_step(k); }
    return div_step(k + 8);
}

/// `*%`: the low 128 bits of the product, the same for signed and unsigned words in two's complement: A0 * B0 in
/// full (mul and umulh), plus the low words of the two cross products in the high word.
fn mul_w_step(k: u32) -> u64 {
    if (k == 0) { return st(I_UMULH, R_S0, R_A0, R_B0, 0); }
    if (k == 1) { return st(I_MUL, R_S1, R_A0, R_B1, 0); }
    if (k == 2) { return st(I_ADDS, R_S0, R_S0, R_S1, 0); }
    if (k == 3) { return st(I_MUL, R_S1, R_A1, R_B0, 0); }
    if (k == 4) { return st(I_ADDS, R_A1, R_S0, R_S1, 0); }
    return st(I_MUL, R_A0, R_A0, R_B0, 0);
}

/// `&`, `|` and `^` (`op` I_AND, I_ORR or I_EOR): word by word.
fn logic_step(op: u8, k: u32) -> u64 {
    if (k == 0) { return st(op, R_A0, R_A0, R_B0, 0); }
    return st(op, R_A1, R_A1, R_B1, 0);
}

/// A checked shift's amount, in B0, below 128, or a trap at the operator's site (Zig's `<< @intCast(n)` panics
/// when the u7 does not hold n). A negative amount is 2^63 or more in B0, so it traps too.
fn shift_check(k: u32) -> u64 {
    if (k == 0) { return st(I_MOVZ, R_S0, 0, 0, 128); }
    if (k == 1) { return st(I_SUBS, R_ZR, R_B0, R_S0, 0); }
    return st(I_TRAP, 0, 0, 0, COND_HS);
}

/// `<<` by n, the bits shifted out dropped: (hi << n | lo >> (64 - n), lo << n) below 64, (lo << (n - 64), 0)
/// from 64 up; ANDS of n with 64 picks one. lslv and lsrv shift by n modulo 64, and `(lo >> 1) >> (63 - n)`
/// is `lo >> (64 - n)` for n of 1 to 63 and 0 for n = 0; `63 - n` modulo 64 is `~n` (orn).
fn shl_step(k: u32) -> u64 {
    if (k == 0) { return st(I_LSLV, R_S0, R_A1, R_B0, 0); }
    if (k == 1) { return st(I_ORN, R_S1, R_ZR, R_B0, 0); }
    if (k == 2) { return st(I_LSR, R_S2, R_A0, 0, 1); }
    if (k == 3) { return st(I_LSRV, R_S1, R_S2, R_S1, 0); }
    if (k == 4) { return st(I_ORR, R_S0, R_S0, R_S1, 0); }
    if (k == 5) { return st(I_LSLV, R_S1, R_A0, R_B0, 0); }
    if (k == 6) { return st(I_MOVZ, R_S2, 0, 0, 64); }
    if (k == 7) { return st(I_ANDS, R_ZR, R_B0, R_S2, 0); }
    if (k == 8) { return st(I_CSEL, R_A1, R_S1, R_S0, COND_NE); }
    return st(I_CSEL, R_A0, R_ZR, R_S1, COND_NE);
}

/// `>>` by n, arithmetic: (lo >> n | hi << (64 - n), hi >> n) below 64, (hi >> (n - 64), the sign) from 64 up.
fn shr_step(k: u32) -> u64 {
    if (k == 0) { return st(I_LSRV, R_S0, R_A0, R_B0, 0); }
    if (k == 1) { return st(I_ORN, R_S1, R_ZR, R_B0, 0); }
    if (k == 2) { return st(I_LSL, R_S2, R_A1, 0, 1); }
    if (k == 3) { return st(I_LSLV, R_S1, R_S2, R_S1, 0); }
    if (k == 4) { return st(I_ORR, R_S0, R_S0, R_S1, 0); }
    if (k == 5) { return st(I_ASRV, R_S1, R_A1, R_B0, 0); }
    if (k == 6) { return st(I_MOVZ, R_S2, 0, 0, 64); }
    if (k == 7) { return st(I_ANDS, R_ZR, R_B0, R_S2, 0); }
    if (k == 8) { return st(I_CSEL, R_A0, R_S1, R_S0, COND_NE); }
    if (k == 9) { return st(I_ASR, R_S2, R_A1, 0, 63); }
    return st(I_CSEL, R_A1, R_S2, R_S1, COND_NE);
}

/// A checked cast to a narrower type: the high word against 0 (`signed` false) or the low word's sign.
fn cast_step(signed: bool, k: u32) -> u64 {
    if (signed and k == 0) { return st(I_ASR, R_S0, R_A0, 0, 63); }
    if (signed and k == 1) { return st(I_SUBS, R_ZR, R_A1, R_S0, 0); }
    if (k == 0) { return st(I_SUBS, R_ZR, R_A1, R_ZR, 0); }
    return st(I_TRAP, 0, 0, 0, COND_NE);
}

/// How many steps program `prog` has.
pub fn steps(prog: u8) -> u32 {
    if (prog == PROG_ADD or prog == PROG_SUB) { return 3; }
    if (prog == PROG_MUL) { return 35; }
    if (prog == PROG_DIV) { return 18; }
    if (prog == PROG_REM) { return 10; }
    if (prog == PROG_MUL_W) { return 6; }
    if (prog == PROG_ADD_W or prog == PROG_SUB_W or prog == PROG_AND or prog == PROG_OR or prog == PROG_XOR) { return 2; }
    if (prog == PROG_SHL) { return 13; }
    if (prog == PROG_SHR) { return 14; }
    if (prog == PROG_SHL_W) { return 10; }
    if (prog == PROG_SHR_W) { return 11; }
    if (prog == PROG_CAST_U) { return 2; }
    if (prog == PROG_CAST_S) { return 3; }
    return 0;
}

/// Step k of program `prog`, packed.
fn step(prog: u8, k: u32) -> u64 {
    if (prog == PROG_ADD or prog == PROG_ADD_W) { return add_step(k); }
    if (prog == PROG_SUB or prog == PROG_SUB_W) { return sub_step(k); }
    if (prog == PROG_MUL) { return mul_step(k); }
    if (prog == PROG_MUL_W) { return mul_w_step(k); }
    if (prog == PROG_REM) { return rem_step(k); }
    if (prog == PROG_AND) { return logic_step(I_AND, k); }
    if (prog == PROG_OR) { return logic_step(I_ORR, k); }
    if (prog == PROG_XOR) { return logic_step(I_EOR, k); }
    if ((prog == PROG_SHL or prog == PROG_SHR) and k < 3) { return shift_check(k); }
    if (prog == PROG_SHL) { return shl_step(k - 3); }
    if (prog == PROG_SHR) { return shr_step(k - 3); }
    if (prog == PROG_SHL_W) { return shl_step(k); }
    if (prog == PROG_SHR_W) { return shr_step(k); }
    if (prog == PROG_CAST_U) { return cast_step(false, k); }
    if (prog == PROG_CAST_S) { return cast_step(true, k); }
    return div_step(k);
}

/// What the glue does with step k: emits its word, branches to a trap site on its condition, or calls the routine.
pub const K_WORD : u8 = 0;
pub const K_TRAP : u8 = 1;
pub const K_CALL : u8 = 2;

pub fn step_kind(prog: u8, k: u32) -> u8 {
    const op : u8 = s_part(step(prog, k), 0);
    if (op == I_TRAP) { return K_TRAP; }
    if (op == I_CALL) { return K_CALL; }
    return K_WORD;
}

/// The site a K_TRAP step branches to, counted from the operator's first site.
pub fn trap_site(prog: u8, k: u32) -> u32 {
    return s_part(step(prog, k), 3) as u32;
}

/// The instruction word of step k, its registers placed by `reg_of`; for a K_TRAP step, its condition.
pub fn step_word(prog: u8, k: u32, first: u8) -> u32 {
    const s : u64 = step(prog, k);
    const op : u8 = s_part(s, 0);
    const d : u8 = reg_of(s_part(s, 1), first);
    const n : u8 = reg_of(s_part(s, 2), first);
    const m : u8 = reg_of(s_part(s, 3), first);
    const x : u32 = s_x(s);
    if (op == I_ADDS) { return adds(true, d, n, m); }
    if (op == I_ADCS) { return adcs(true, d, n, m); }
    if (op == I_SUBS) { return subs(true, d, n, m); }
    if (op == I_SBCS) { return sbcs(true, d, n, m); }
    if (op == I_EOR) { return logic_reg(true, LogOp.Eor, false, d, n, m); }
    if (op == I_ORR) { return logic_reg(true, LogOp.Orr, false, d, n, m); }
    if (op == I_AND) { return logic_reg(true, LogOp.And, false, d, n, m); }
    if (op == I_ORN) { return logic_reg(true, LogOp.Orr, true, d, n, m); }
    if (op == I_ASR) { return asr_imm(true, d, n, x); }
    if (op == I_MUL) { return mul(true, d, n, m); }
    if (op == I_UMULH) { return umulh(d, n, m); }
    if (op == I_MOVZ) { return movz(true, d, x & 65535, x / 65536); }
    if (op == I_CCMP and x / 16 == COND_NE) { return ccmp(true, n, m, x & 15, Cond.Ne); }
    if (op == I_CCMP) { return ccmp(true, n, m, x & 15, Cond.Eq); }
    if (op == I_LSLV) { return lslv(true, d, n, m); }
    if (op == I_LSRV) { return lsrv(true, d, n, m); }
    if (op == I_ASRV) { return asrv(true, d, n, m); }
    if (op == I_LSL) { return lsl_imm(true, d, n, x); }
    if (op == I_LSR) { return lsr_imm(true, d, n, x); }
    if (op == I_ANDS) { return logic_reg(true, LogOp.Ands, false, d, n, m); }
    if (op == I_CSEL) { return csel(true, d, n, m, Cond.Ne); }
    return x;
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- the flags, modelled

/// NZCV as four bits.
const FLAG_N : u32 = 8;
const FLAG_Z : u32 = 4;
const FLAG_C : u32 = 2;
const FLAG_V : u32 = 1;

/// x - y - borrow modulo 2^64, for a borrow of 0 or 1.
fn sub_word(x: u64, y: u64, borrow: u64) -> u64 {
    const d : u64 = t27b_i128_diff(x, y);
    if (borrow == 0) { return d; }
    if (d == 0) { return MAX64; }
    return d - 1;
}

/// The flags SUBS x, y (borrow 0) or SBCS x, y (borrow 1 when C is clear) leave: N the sign of the result, Z
/// a zero result, C no borrow out, V a signed overflow.
fn sub_flags(x: u64, y: u64, borrow: u64) -> u32 {
    const d : u64 = sub_word(x, y, borrow);
    var f : u32 = 0;
    if (d >= SIGN64) { f = f | FLAG_N; }
    if (d == 0) { f = f | FLAG_Z; }
    if (x > y or (x == y and borrow == 0)) { f = f | FLAG_C; }
    const sx : bool = x >= SIGN64;
    const sy : bool = y >= SIGN64;
    const sd : bool = d >= SIGN64;
    if (sx != sy and sd != sx) { f = f | FLAG_V; }
    return f;
}

/// x + y + carry modulo 2^64, for a carry of 0 or 1: x minus the two's complement of y, plus the carry.
fn add_word(x: u64, y: u64, carry: u64) -> u64 {
    const s : u64 = t27b_i128_diff(x, t27b_i128_diff(0, y));
    if (carry == 0) { return s; }
    if (s == MAX64) { return 0; }
    return s + 1;
}

/// The flags ADDS x, y (carry 0) or ADCS x, y (carry C) leave: N, Z, C the carry out, V a signed overflow.
fn add_flags(x: u64, y: u64, carry: u64) -> u32 {
    const s : u64 = add_word(x, y, carry);
    var f : u32 = 0;
    if (s >= SIGN64) { f = f | FLAG_N; }
    if (s == 0) { f = f | FLAG_Z; }
    if (x > MAX64 - y or (x == MAX64 - y and carry == 1)) { f = f | FLAG_C; }
    const sx : bool = x >= SIGN64;
    if (sx == (y >= SIGN64) and (s >= SIGN64) != sx) { f = f | FLAG_V; }
    return f;
}

/// The low (part 0) or high (part 1) word of the 128-bit product x * y, from 32-bit halves: MUL and UMULH.
fn mul_word(x: u64, y: u64, part: u32) -> u64 {
    const x1 : u64 = x >> 32;
    const x0 : u64 = x & LOW32;
    const y1 : u64 = y >> 32;
    const y0 : u64 = y & LOW32;
    const p00 : u64 = x0 * y0;
    const p01 : u64 = x0 * y1;
    const p10 : u64 = x1 * y0;
    const mid : u64 = (p00 >> 32) + (p01 & LOW32) + (p10 & LOW32);
    if (part == 0) { return ((mid & LOW32) << 32) | (p00 & LOW32); }
    return x1 * y1 + (p01 >> 32) + (p10 >> 32) + (mid >> 32);
}

/// x >> k, arithmetic: the sign copied into the k bits shifted in.
fn asr_word(x: u64, k: u32) -> u64 {
    if (x < SIGN64) { return x >> k; }
    return (x >> k) | (MAX64 ^ (MAX64 >> k));
}

/// Does condition `c` (one of the COND_ values) hold under flags `f`?
fn cond_holds(c: u32, f: u32) -> bool {
    const z : bool = (f & FLAG_Z) != 0;
    const n_is_v : bool = ((f & FLAG_N) != 0) == ((f & FLAG_V) != 0);
    if (c == COND_EQ) { return z; }
    if (c == COND_NE) { return z == false; }
    if (c == COND_HS) { return (f & FLAG_C) != 0; }
    if (c == COND_LO) { return (f & FLAG_C) == 0; }
    if (c == COND_MI) { return (f & FLAG_N) != 0; }
    if (c == COND_VS) { return (f & FLAG_V) != 0; }
    if (c == COND_GE) { return n_is_v; }
    return n_is_v == false;
}

/// The flags after comparison step `s` on the words x and y, from the flags `f` the step before left.
fn step_flags(s: u8, x: u64, y: u64, f: u32) -> u32 {
    if (s == STEP_CMP) { return sub_flags(x, y, 0); }
    if (s == STEP_CCMP) {
        if (cond_holds(COND_EQ, f)) { return sub_flags(x, y, 0); }
        return CCMP_NZCV;
    }
    if ((f & FLAG_C) != 0) { return sub_flags(x, y, 0); }
    return sub_flags(x, y, 1);
}

/// `x op y` for the pairs (x_lo, x_hi) and (y_lo, y_hi), by the steps, the exchange and the condition above.
pub fn holds(op: u8, x_lo: u64, x_hi: u64, y_lo: u64, y_hi: u64) -> bool {
    var a_lo : u64 = x_lo;
    var a_hi : u64 = x_hi;
    var b_lo : u64 = y_lo;
    var b_hi : u64 = y_hi;
    if (cmp_swaps(op)) {
        a_lo = y_lo;
        a_hi = y_hi;
        b_lo = x_lo;
        b_hi = x_hi;
    }
    const f0 : u32 = step_flags(cmp_step(op, 0), a_lo, b_lo, 0);
    const f1 : u32 = step_flags(cmp_step(op, 1), a_hi, b_hi, f0);
    return cond_holds(cmp_cond(op), f1);
}

/// The flags ANDS leaves: N the sign of the result, Z a zero result, C and V clear.
fn logic_flags(v: u64) -> u32 {
    var f : u32 = 0;
    if (v >= SIGN64) { f = f | FLAG_N; }
    if (v == 0) { f = f | FLAG_Z; }
    return f;
}

/// The value step `op` writes, from its operands' values vn and vm, its x and the flags f before it.
fn value_of(op: u8, vn: u64, vm: u64, x: u32, f: u32) -> u64 {
    var c : u64 = 0;
    if ((f & FLAG_C) != 0) { c = 1; }
    if (op == I_LSLV) { return vn << ((vm & 63) as u32); }
    if (op == I_LSRV) { return vn >> ((vm & 63) as u32); }
    if (op == I_ASRV) { return asr_word(vn, (vm & 63) as u32); }
    if (op == I_LSL) { return vn << x; }
    if (op == I_LSR) { return vn >> x; }
    if (op == I_ANDS) { return vn & vm; }
    if (op == I_CSEL and cond_holds(x, f)) { return vn; }
    if (op == I_CSEL) { return vm; }
    if (op == I_ADDS) { return add_word(vn, vm, 0); }
    if (op == I_ADCS) { return add_word(vn, vm, c); }
    if (op == I_SUBS) { return sub_word(vn, vm, 0); }
    if (op == I_SBCS) { return sub_word(vn, vm, 1 - c); }
    if (op == I_EOR) { return vn ^ vm; }
    if (op == I_ORR) { return vn | vm; }
    if (op == I_AND) { return vn & vm; }
    if (op == I_ORN) { return vn | (vm ^ MAX64); }
    if (op == I_ASR) { return asr_word(vn, x); }
    if (op == I_MUL) { return mul_word(vn, vm, 0); }
    if (op == I_UMULH) { return mul_word(vn, vm, 1); }
    return ((x & 65535) as u64) << (16 * (x / 65536));
}

/// The flags step `op` leaves, from the flags f before it: adds, adcs, subs and sbcs set them, the others keep them.
fn flags_of(op: u8, vn: u64, vm: u64, f: u32) -> u32 {
    var c : u64 = 0;
    if ((f & FLAG_C) != 0) { c = 1; }
    if (op == I_ADDS) { return add_flags(vn, vm, 0); }
    if (op == I_ADCS) { return add_flags(vn, vm, c); }
    if (op == I_SUBS) { return sub_flags(vn, vm, 0); }
    if (op == I_SBCS) { return sub_flags(vn, vm, 1 - c); }
    if (op == I_ANDS) { return logic_flags(vn & vm); }
    return f;
}

/// How a model run ends: `trap` RUN_OK and the result's words, or the site it trapped at, plus 1.
pub const PairRun = struct {
    trap : u32,
    lo : u64,
    hi : u64,
};
pub const RUN_OK : u32 = 0;

/// Program `prog` on the operands (a_lo, a_hi) and (b_lo, b_hi), step by step, on a model of the twelve step
/// registers and NZCV. R_ZR reads 0 and ignores what is written to it; I_CALL runs the routine's words (the
/// remainder's for PROG_REM, the quotient's otherwise).
pub fn run_steps(prog: u8, a_lo: u64, a_hi: u64, b_lo: u64, b_hi: u64) -> PairRun {
    var x : [12]u64 = [0] ** 12;
    x[0] = a_lo;
    x[1] = a_hi;
    x[2] = b_lo;
    x[3] = b_hi;
    var f : u32 = 0;
    var k : u32 = 0;
    while (k < steps(prog)) {
        const s : u64 = step(prog, k);
        const op : u8 = s_part(s, 0);
        const d : u8 = s_part(s, 1);
        const vn : u64 = x[s_part(s, 2)];
        const vm : u64 = x[s_part(s, 3)];
        if (op == I_TRAP) {
            if (cond_holds(s_x(s), f)) { return PairRun{ .trap = trap_site(prog, k) + 1, .lo = 0, .hi = 0 }; }
        } else if (op == I_CALL) {
            const q : t27b_i128_words = t27b_i128_quot(x[R_X0], x[R_X1], x[R_X2], x[R_X3], prog == PROG_REM);
            x[R_X0] = q.lo;
            x[R_X1] = q.hi;
        } else if (op == I_CCMP) {
            if (cond_holds(s_x(s) / 16, f)) { f = sub_flags(vn, vm, 0); } else { f = s_x(s) & 15; }
        } else {
            const v : u64 = value_of(op, vn, vm, s_x(s), f);
            f = flags_of(op, vn, vm, f);
            if (d != R_ZR) { x[d] = v; }
        }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    return PairRun{ .trap = RUN_OK, .lo = x[R_A0], .hi = x[R_A1] };
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- the division routine

/// The routine's names in this file, and in a program it is spliced into (libm_plan.t27's PORT and HELPER).
pub const PORT : str = "t27b_i128_";
pub const HELPER : str = "__t27b_i128_";
/// A program that names one of these builtins gets the routines spliced in.
pub const BUILTINS : str = "@divTrunc @rem";
/// The fns the I_CALL steps of PROG_DIV and PROG_REM call, by their spliced names.
pub const DIV_ROUTINE : str = "__t27b_i128_div";
pub const REM_ROUTINE : str = "__t27b_i128_rem";

const t27b_i128_max64 : u64 = 18446744073709551615;
const t27b_i128_sign64 : u64 = 9223372036854775808;
const t27b_i128_low32 : u64 = 4294967295;
const t27b_i128_two64 : i128 = 18446744073709551616;

/// Two words, the low one first.
pub const t27b_i128_words = struct {
    lo : u64,
    hi : u64,
};

/// x - y modulo 2^64.
pub fn t27b_i128_diff(t27b_x: u64, t27b_y: u64) -> u64 {
    if (t27b_x >= t27b_y) { return t27b_x - t27b_y; }
    return (t27b_i128_max64 - t27b_y) + t27b_x + 1;
}

/// Word `t27b_part` (0 the low one) of 0 minus the pair (t27b_lo, t27b_hi), modulo 2^128: the low word negated,
/// and the high word's complement plus the carry out of the low word, which is 1 exactly when the low word is 0.
pub fn t27b_i128_neg(t27b_lo: u64, t27b_hi: u64, t27b_part: u32) -> u64 {
    if (t27b_part == 0) { return t27b_i128_diff(0, t27b_lo); }
    if (t27b_lo == 0) { return t27b_i128_diff(0, t27b_hi); }
    return t27b_i128_max64 - t27b_hi;
}

/// The quotient of the magnitudes n = (t27b_nl, t27b_nh) and d = (t27b_dl, t27b_dh), or their remainder when
/// `t27b_rem`, d not 0 and both at most 2^127: one division of words when both fit 64 bits; when d fits 32 bits,
/// the high word of n divided first and the low word in two 32-bit digits, each partial dividend below d * 2^32,
/// the last digit's remainder the remainder; otherwise binary long division, the remainder below d and so below
/// 2^127 before each doubling.
fn t27b_i128_udiv(t27b_nl: u64, t27b_nh: u64, t27b_dl: u64, t27b_dh: u64, t27b_rem: bool) -> t27b_i128_words {
    if (t27b_dh == 0 and t27b_nh == 0 and t27b_rem) {
        return t27b_i128_words{ .lo = t27b_nl % t27b_dl, .hi = 0 };
    }
    if (t27b_dh == 0 and t27b_nh == 0) {
        return t27b_i128_words{ .lo = t27b_nl / t27b_dl, .hi = 0 };
    }
    if (t27b_dh == 0 and t27b_dl <= t27b_i128_low32) {
        const t27b_u1 : u64 = ((t27b_nh % t27b_dl) << 32) | (t27b_nl >> 32);
        const t27b_u0 : u64 = ((t27b_u1 % t27b_dl) << 32) | (t27b_nl & t27b_i128_low32);
        if (t27b_rem) { return t27b_i128_words{ .lo = t27b_u0 % t27b_dl, .hi = 0 }; }
        return t27b_i128_words{ .lo = ((t27b_u1 / t27b_dl) << 32) | (t27b_u0 / t27b_dl), .hi = t27b_nh / t27b_dl };
    }
    var t27b_rl : u64 = 0;
    var t27b_rh : u64 = 0;
    var t27b_ql : u64 = 0;
    var t27b_qh : u64 = 0;
    var t27b_k : u32 = 128;
    while (t27b_k > 0) {
        t27b_k = t27b_k - 1;
        var t27b_b : u64 = 0;
        if (t27b_k >= 64) { t27b_b = (t27b_nh >> (t27b_k - 64)) & 1; } else { t27b_b = (t27b_nl >> t27b_k) & 1; }
        t27b_rh = (t27b_rh << 1) | (t27b_rl >> 63);
        t27b_rl = (t27b_rl << 1) | t27b_b;
        t27b_qh = (t27b_qh << 1) | (t27b_ql >> 63);
        t27b_ql = t27b_ql << 1;
        if (t27b_rh > t27b_dh or (t27b_rh == t27b_dh and t27b_rl >= t27b_dl)) {
            if (t27b_rl < t27b_dl) { t27b_rh = t27b_rh - 1; }
            t27b_rh = t27b_rh - t27b_dh;
            t27b_rl = t27b_i128_diff(t27b_rl, t27b_dl);
            t27b_ql = t27b_ql | 1;
        }
    }
    if (t27b_rem) { return t27b_i128_words{ .lo = t27b_rl, .hi = t27b_rh }; }
    return t27b_i128_words{ .lo = t27b_ql, .hi = t27b_qh };
}

/// The words of `@divTrunc(a, b)`, or of `@rem(a, b)` when `t27b_rem`, two's complement, from the words of a and
/// b: the quotient of the magnitudes, negated when exactly one operand is negative; the remainder of the
/// magnitudes, negated when a is (it takes the dividend's sign). b is not 0, and a quotient is not minInt / -1
/// (DIV steps 0 to 10); minInt % -1 is the remainder of 2^127 by 1, 0.
pub fn t27b_i128_quot(t27b_al: u64, t27b_ah: u64, t27b_bl: u64, t27b_bh: u64, t27b_rem: bool) -> t27b_i128_words {
    const t27b_an : bool = t27b_ah >= t27b_i128_sign64;
    const t27b_bn : bool = t27b_bh >= t27b_i128_sign64;
    var t27b_nl : u64 = t27b_al;
    var t27b_nh : u64 = t27b_ah;
    if (t27b_an) {
        t27b_nl = t27b_i128_neg(t27b_al, t27b_ah, 0);
        t27b_nh = t27b_i128_neg(t27b_al, t27b_ah, 1);
    }
    var t27b_dl : u64 = t27b_bl;
    var t27b_dh : u64 = t27b_bh;
    if (t27b_bn) {
        t27b_dl = t27b_i128_neg(t27b_bl, t27b_bh, 0);
        t27b_dh = t27b_i128_neg(t27b_bl, t27b_bh, 1);
    }
    const t27b_q : t27b_i128_words = t27b_i128_udiv(t27b_nl, t27b_nh, t27b_dl, t27b_dh, t27b_rem);
    if (t27b_rem and t27b_an == false) { return t27b_q; }
    if (t27b_rem == false and t27b_an == t27b_bn) { return t27b_q; }
    return t27b_i128_words{ .lo = t27b_i128_neg(t27b_q.lo, t27b_q.hi, 0), .hi = t27b_i128_neg(t27b_q.lo, t27b_q.hi, 1) };
}

/// The i128 whose two's complement words are (t27b_lo, t27b_hi): the high word read as signed, times 2^64, plus
/// the low word; no partial value leaves i128.
pub fn t27b_i128_join(t27b_lo: u64, t27b_hi: u64) -> i128 {
    var t27b_h : i128 = @intCast(t27b_hi);
    if (t27b_hi >= t27b_i128_sign64) { t27b_h = t27b_h - t27b_i128_two64; }
    const t27b_l : i128 = @intCast(t27b_lo);
    return t27b_h * t27b_i128_two64 + t27b_l;
}

/// `@divTrunc(a, b)` of two i128s given as words, the low word first. t27b calls it as DIV_ROUTINE after DIV
/// steps 0 to 10: the words in x0 to x3, as AAPCS64 passes two i128 arguments, the quotient back in x0:x1.
pub fn t27b_i128_div(t27b_al: u64, t27b_ah: u64, t27b_bl: u64, t27b_bh: u64) -> i128 {
    const t27b_q : t27b_i128_words = t27b_i128_quot(t27b_al, t27b_ah, t27b_bl, t27b_bh, false);
    return t27b_i128_join(t27b_q.lo, t27b_q.hi);
}

/// `@rem(a, b)` of two i128s given as words. t27b calls it as REM_ROUTINE after REM steps 0 to 2, as it calls
/// t27b_i128_div; the remainder back in x0:x1.
pub fn t27b_i128_rem(t27b_al: u64, t27b_ah: u64, t27b_bl: u64, t27b_bh: u64) -> i128 {
    const t27b_r : t27b_i128_words = t27b_i128_quot(t27b_al, t27b_ah, t27b_bl, t27b_bh, true);
    return t27b_i128_join(t27b_r.lo, t27b_r.hi);
}

// ---------------------------------------------------------------- tests

/// How many sample integers the tests compare, each with every other.
const SAMPLES : u32 = 19;

const MAX128 : i128 = 170141183460469231731687303715884105727;
const MIN128 : i128 = 0 - 170141183460469231731687303715884105727 - 1;

/// Sample integer i as its sign (part 0: 1 when negative), its magnitude's high word (part 1) and its
/// magnitude's low word (part 2): 0, 1, -1, -52, 7286977268806824, 2^63, -2^63, 2^64 - 1, -(2^64 - 1), 2^64,
/// -2^64, 2^64 + 1, the greatest i128, the least i128 plus 1, the least i128, 2^32 - 1, -2^32, 3 and 2^96 + 7.
fn sample(i: u32, part: u32) -> u64 {
    var neg : u64 = 0;
    var hi : u64 = 0;
    var lo : u64 = 0;
    if (i == 1) { lo = 1; }
    if (i == 2) { neg = 1; lo = 1; }
    if (i == 3) { neg = 1; lo = 52; }
    if (i == 4) { lo = 7286977268806824; }
    if (i == 5) { lo = SIGN64; }
    if (i == 6) { neg = 1; lo = SIGN64; }
    if (i == 7) { lo = MAX64; }
    if (i == 8) { neg = 1; lo = MAX64; }
    if (i == 9) { hi = 1; }
    if (i == 10) { neg = 1; hi = 1; }
    if (i == 11) { hi = 1; lo = 1; }
    if (i == 12) { hi = SIGN64 - 1; lo = MAX64; }
    if (i == 13) { neg = 1; hi = SIGN64 - 1; lo = MAX64; }
    if (i == 14) { neg = 1; hi = SIGN64; }
    if (i == 15) { lo = LOW32; }
    if (i == 16) { neg = 1; lo = LOW32 + 1; }
    if (i == 17) { lo = 3; }
    if (i == 18) { hi = LOW32 + 1; lo = 7; }
    if (part == 0) { return neg; }
    if (part == 1) { return hi; }
    return lo;
}

/// Word k (0 low, 1 high) of sample i, by the split above.
fn sample_word(i: u32, k: u32) -> u64 {
    const neg : bool = sample(i, 0) == 1;
    if (k == 0) { return lit_lo(neg, sample(i, 2)); }
    return lit_hi(neg, sample(i, 2), sample(i, 1));
}

/// The order of samples i and j from their signs and magnitudes: 0 less, 1 equal, 2 greater.
fn order(i: u32, j: u32) -> u8 {
    const ni : bool = sample(i, 0) == 1;
    const nj : bool = sample(j, 0) == 1;
    if (ni and nj == false) { return 0; }
    if (nj and ni == false) { return 2; }
    var m : u8 = 1;
    if (sample(i, 1) != sample(j, 1)) {
        if (sample(i, 1) < sample(j, 1)) { m = 0; } else { m = 2; }
    } else if (sample(i, 2) != sample(j, 2)) {
        if (sample(i, 2) < sample(j, 2)) { m = 0; } else { m = 2; }
    }
    if (ni) { return 2 - m; }
    return m;
}

/// Whether `op` holds for two integers in order `ord`.
fn expected(op: u8, ord: u8) -> bool {
    if (op == EQ) { return ord == 1; }
    if (op == NE) { return ord != 1; }
    if (op == LT) { return ord == 0; }
    if (op == LE) { return ord != 2; }
    if (op == GT) { return ord == 2; }
    return ord != 0;
}

/// Sample i as an i128.
fn sample_value(i: u32) -> i128 {
    return t27b_i128_join(sample_word(i, 0), sample_word(i, 1));
}

/// Is the sum of samples i and j an i128? Asked without forming it.
fn sum_fits(i: u32, j: u32) -> bool {
    const x : i128 = sample_value(i);
    const y : i128 = sample_value(j);
    if (y > 0) { return x <= MAX128 - y; }
    return x >= MIN128 - y;
}

/// Is sample i minus sample j an i128?
fn difference_fits(i: u32, j: u32) -> bool {
    const x : i128 = sample_value(i);
    const y : i128 = sample_value(j);
    if (y < 0) { return x <= MAX128 + y; }
    return x >= MIN128 + y;
}

/// Is the product of samples i and j an i128? Each bound divided by one operand, rounded toward zero, bounds the
/// other.
fn product_fits(i: u32, j: u32) -> bool {
    const x : i128 = sample_value(i);
    const y : i128 = sample_value(j);
    if (x == 0 or y == 0) { return true; }
    if (x > 0 and y > 0) { return x <= @divTrunc(MAX128, y); }
    if (x > 0) { return y >= @divTrunc(MIN128, x); }
    if (y > 0) { return x >= @divTrunc(MIN128, y); }
    return y >= @divTrunc(MAX128, x);
}

test the_result_is_x0_then_x1_and_a_home_is_sixteen_aligned_bytes {
    assert RET_LO == 0;
    assert RET_HI == 1;
    assert HI_OFF == 8;
    assert HOME_WORDS * 8 == BYTES;
    assert BYTES == 16;
    assert ALIGN == 16;
    assert std.mem.eql(u8, NAME, "i128");
    assert std.mem.eql(u8, REFUSED, "type i128");
}

test a_pair_argument_starts_at_an_even_register_and_fits_up_to_x6 {
    assert pair_first(0) == 0;
    assert pair_first(1) == 2;
    assert pair_first(2) == 2;
    assert pair_first(5) == 6;
    assert pair_first(6) == 6;
    assert pair_first(7) == 8;
    assert pair_in_regs(0);
    assert pair_in_regs(5);
    assert pair_in_regs(6);
    assert pair_in_regs(7) == false;
    assert pair_in_regs(8) == false;
    // eval_arith.t27's `arith(op: u8, bits: u32, signed: bool, boolean: bool, a: i128, b: i128)`: x0 to x3, then
    // a in x4:x5 and b in x6:x7; its hidden result pointer goes on the stack.
    assert arg_reg(4, true) == 4;
    assert arg_next(4, true) == 6;
    assert arg_reg(6, true) == 6;
    assert arg_next(6, true) == 8;
    assert arg_reg(8, false) == 8;
    // `holds(op: u8, a: i128, b: i128)`: a skips x1 for x2:x3.
    assert arg_reg(1, true) == 2;
    assert arg_next(2, true) == 4;
    // A scalar keeps its register; a pair that does not fit goes on the stack and takes every later one with it.
    assert arg_reg(3, false) == 3;
    assert arg_next(3, false) == 4;
    assert arg_reg(7, true) == 8;
    assert arg_next(8, true) == 9;
    assert arg_reg(9, true) == 9;
}

test a_pair_in_memory_is_one_ldp_or_stp {
    assert pair_imm(0);
    assert pair_imm(16);
    assert pair_imm(504);
    assert pair_imm(512) == false;
    assert pair_imm(12) == false;
    // ldp x9, x10, [x17, #16]; stp x16, x8, [x17]; stp x2, x3, [sp, #32]; from GNU as on the t27c lab.
    assert pair_word(true, 9, 10, 17, 16) == 0xa9412a29;
    assert pair_word(false, 16, 8, 17, 0) == 0xa9002230;
    assert pair_word(false, 2, 3, 31, 32) == 0xa9020fe2;
}

test a_literal_splits_into_its_twos_complement_words {
    // 7286977268806824 and -52, the literals phi_f64_literals returns.
    assert lit_lo(false, 7286977268806824) == 7286977268806824;
    assert lit_hi(false, 7286977268806824, 0) == 0;
    assert lit_lo(true, 52) == 18446744073709551564;
    assert lit_hi(true, 52, 0) == MAX64;
    assert lit_lo(false, 0) == 0;
    assert lit_hi(false, 0, 0) == 0;
    // 2^64 and -2^64: the carry out of a zero low word.
    assert lit_lo(false, 0) == 0;
    assert lit_hi(false, 0, 1) == 1;
    assert lit_lo(true, 0) == 0;
    assert lit_hi(true, 0, 1) == MAX64;
    // -(2^64 + 1): no carry.
    assert lit_lo(true, 1) == MAX64;
    assert lit_hi(true, 1, 1) == MAX64 - 1;
    // The greatest i128, and the least, whose magnitude 2^127 is its own two's complement.
    assert lit_lo(false, MAX64) == MAX64;
    assert lit_hi(false, MAX64, SIGN64 - 1) == SIGN64 - 1;
    assert lit_lo(true, 0) == 0;
    assert lit_hi(true, 0, SIGN64) == SIGN64;
    // The least plus 1.
    assert lit_lo(true, MAX64) == 1;
    assert lit_hi(true, MAX64, SIGN64 - 1) == SIGN64;
}

test equality_is_cmp_then_ccmp_and_order_is_cmp_then_sbcs {
    var op : u8 = 0;
    while (op < 6) {
        assert cmp_step(op, 0) == STEP_CMP;
        op = op + 1;
    }
    assert cmp_step(EQ, 1) == STEP_CCMP;
    assert cmp_step(NE, 1) == STEP_CCMP;
    assert cmp_step(LT, 1) == STEP_SBCS;
    assert cmp_step(LE, 1) == STEP_SBCS;
    assert cmp_step(GT, 1) == STEP_SBCS;
    assert cmp_step(GE, 1) == STEP_SBCS;
    assert cmp_swaps(EQ) == false;
    assert cmp_swaps(NE) == false;
    assert cmp_swaps(LT) == false;
    assert cmp_swaps(GE) == false;
    assert cmp_swaps(GT);
    assert cmp_swaps(LE);
    assert cmp_cond(EQ) == COND_EQ;
    assert cmp_cond(NE) == COND_NE;
    assert cmp_cond(LT) == COND_LT;
    assert cmp_cond(GT) == COND_LT;
    assert cmp_cond(GE) == COND_GE;
    assert cmp_cond(LE) == COND_GE;
    assert CCMP_NZCV == 0;
}

test the_flags_of_one_word {
    // 5 - 3: C set (no borrow); 3 - 5: N, borrow; 0 - 0: Z and C; 2^63 - 1: V (the least i64 minus 1).
    assert sub_flags(5, 3, 0) == FLAG_C;
    assert sub_flags(3, 5, 0) == FLAG_N;
    assert sub_flags(0, 0, 0) == FLAG_Z + FLAG_C;
    assert sub_flags(SIGN64, 1, 0) == FLAG_C + FLAG_V;
    // With a borrow: 5 - 5 - 1 borrows; 6 - 5 - 1 is zero with no borrow.
    assert sub_flags(5, 5, 1) == FLAG_N;
    assert sub_flags(6, 5, 1) == FLAG_Z + FLAG_C;
    assert sub_word(0, 1, 0) == MAX64;
    assert sub_word(0, 0, 1) == MAX64;
    assert sub_word(MAX64, 0, 1) == MAX64 - 1;
    // Sums: 2^64 - 1 + 1 carries to 0; 2^63 - 1 + 1 overflows to the least i64; a carry in.
    assert add_word(MAX64, 1, 0) == 0;
    assert add_flags(MAX64, 1, 0) == FLAG_Z + FLAG_C;
    assert add_flags(SIGN64 - 1, 1, 0) == FLAG_N + FLAG_V;
    assert add_word(MAX64, 0, 1) == 0;
    assert add_flags(MAX64, 0, 1) == FLAG_Z + FLAG_C;
    assert add_word(2, 3, 1) == 6;
    assert add_flags(SIGN64, SIGN64, 0) == FLAG_Z + FLAG_C + FLAG_V;
    // MUL and UMULH, and asr.
    assert mul_word(MAX64, MAX64, 0) == 1;
    assert mul_word(MAX64, MAX64, 1) == MAX64 - 1;
    assert mul_word(LOW32 + 1, LOW32 + 1, 0) == 0;
    assert mul_word(LOW32 + 1, LOW32 + 1, 1) == 1;
    assert mul_word(7286977268806824, 52, 0) == 378922817977954848;
    assert mul_word(7286977268806824, 52, 1) == 0;
    assert asr_word(SIGN64, 63) == MAX64;
    assert asr_word(SIGN64 - 1, 63) == 0;
    assert asr_word(MAX64 - 15, 2) == MAX64 - 3;
}

test the_two_steps_order_every_pair_of_samples {
    var i : u32 = 0;
    var checked : u32 = 0;
    while (i < SAMPLES) {
        var j : u32 = 0;
        while (j < SAMPLES) {
            const ord : u8 = order(i, j);
            var op : u8 = 0;
            while (op < 6) {
                assert holds(op, sample_word(i, 0), sample_word(i, 1), sample_word(j, 0), sample_word(j, 1)) == expected(op, ord);
                checked = checked + 1;
                op = op + 1;
            }
            j = j + 1;
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    assert checked == SAMPLES * SAMPLES * 6;
}

test the_samples_are_distinct_and_ordered_as_listed_by_sign_and_size {
    // -1 < 0 < 1, -2^64 < -(2^64 - 1), the least i128 below everything, the greatest above.
    assert order(2, 0) == 0;
    assert order(0, 1) == 0;
    assert order(10, 8) == 0;
    assert order(14, 13) == 0;
    assert order(12, 11) == 2;
    var i : u32 = 0;
    while (i < SAMPLES) {
        var j : u32 = 0;
        while (j < SAMPLES) {
            if (i != j) { assert order(i, j) != 1; }
            assert order(i, j) == 2 - order(j, i);
            j = j + 1;
        }
        assert order(14, i) == 0 or i == 14;
        assert order(12, i) == 2 or i == 12;
        i = i + 1;
    }
}

test the_overflow_condition_of_one_register {
    assert overflow_cond(true, false) == COND_VS;
    assert overflow_cond(true, true) == COND_VS;
    assert overflow_cond(false, true) == COND_LO;
    assert overflow_cond(false, false) == COND_HS;
    assert cond_holds(COND_LO, 0);
    assert cond_holds(COND_HS, FLAG_C);
    assert cond_holds(COND_VS, FLAG_V);
    assert cond_holds(COND_MI, FLAG_N);
    assert cond_holds(COND_MI, FLAG_C) == false;
}

test a_program_for_each_operator_but_the_wrapping_division {
    assert program(OP_ADD) == PROG_ADD;
    assert program(OP_SUB) == PROG_SUB;
    assert program(OP_MUL) == PROG_MUL;
    assert program(OP_DIV) == PROG_DIV;
    assert program(OP_ADD_W) == PROG_ADD_W;
    assert program(OP_SUB_W) == PROG_SUB_W;
    assert program(OP_MUL_W) == PROG_MUL_W;
    assert program(OP_DIV_W) == PROG_NONE;
    assert program(OP_REM) == PROG_REM;
    assert program(OP_AND) == PROG_AND;
    assert program(OP_OR) == PROG_OR;
    assert program(OP_XOR) == PROG_XOR;
    assert program(OP_SHL) == PROG_SHL;
    assert program(OP_SHR) == PROG_SHR;
    assert program(OP_SHL_W) == PROG_SHL_W;
    assert program(OP_SHR_W) == PROG_SHR_W;
    assert program(16) == PROG_NONE;
    assert cast_program(false, true) == PROG_CAST_U;
    assert cast_program(true, true) == PROG_CAST_S;
    assert cast_program(true, false) == PROG_TRUNC;
    assert steps(PROG_NONE) == 0;
    assert steps(PROG_TRUNC) == 0;
    assert calls(PROG_DIV);
    assert calls(PROG_REM);
    assert calls(PROG_MUL) == false;
    assert std.mem.eql(u8, routine(PROG_DIV), DIV_ROUTINE);
    assert std.mem.eql(u8, routine(PROG_REM), REM_ROUTINE);
    assert routine(PROG_SHL).len == 0;
    // A checked program traps at one step at least and a wrapping or bitwise one at none; DIV and REM call their
    // routine once; every step names only the step registers, and a csel only NE.
    var prog : u8 = PROG_ADD;
    while (prog <= PROG_LAST) {
        var k : u32 = 0;
        var traps : u32 = 0;
        var calls_seen : u32 = 0;
        while (k < steps(prog)) {
            if (step_kind(prog, k) == K_TRAP) { traps = traps + 1; }
            if (step_kind(prog, k) == K_CALL) { calls_seen = calls_seen + 1; }
            if (s_part(step(prog, k), 0) == I_CSEL) { assert s_x(step(prog, k)) == COND_NE; }
            assert s_part(step(prog, k), 1) <= R_X3;
            assert s_part(step(prog, k), 2) <= R_X3;
            assert s_part(step(prog, k), 3) <= R_X3;
            k = k + 1;
        }
        const checked : bool = prog <= PROG_DIV or prog == PROG_REM or prog == PROG_SHL or prog == PROG_SHR or prog == PROG_CAST_U or prog == PROG_CAST_S;
        assert (traps >= 1) == checked;
        assert (calls_seen == 1) == calls(prog);
        prog = prog + 1;
    }
    assert trap_site(PROG_DIV, 2) == 0;
    assert trap_site(PROG_DIV, 10) == 1;
    assert trap_site(PROG_REM, 2) == 0;
    assert trap_site(PROG_SHL, 2) == 0;
    assert step_kind(PROG_REM, 7) == K_CALL;
}

test the_step_registers_are_temps_scratch_zero_and_arguments {
    assert reg_of(R_A0, 9) == 9;
    assert reg_of(R_B1, 9) == 12;
    assert reg_of(R_A1, 11) == 12;
    assert reg_of(R_S0, 9) == 8;
    assert reg_of(R_S1, 9) == 16;
    assert reg_of(R_S2, 9) == 17;
    assert reg_of(R_ZR, 9) == 31;
    assert reg_of(R_X0, 9) == 0;
    assert reg_of(R_X3, 12) == 3;
}

// Words from GNU as (aarch64-linux-gnu-as, then objdump -d) on the t27c lab, the operands in x9 to x12.
test the_step_words_match_gas {
    // adds x9, x9, x11; adcs x10, x10, x12; subs x9, x9, x11; sbcs x10, x10, x12
    assert step_word(PROG_ADD, 0, 9) == 0xab0b0129;
    assert step_word(PROG_ADD, 1, 9) == 0xba0c014a;
    assert step_word(PROG_SUB, 0, 9) == 0xeb0b0129;
    assert step_word(PROG_SUB, 1, 9) == 0xfa0c014a;
    // b.vs: the condition
    assert step_word(PROG_ADD, 2, 9) == COND_VS;
    // asr x8, x10, #63; eor x9, x9, x8; cmp x10, xzr; ccmp x12, xzr, #4, ne; umulh x16, x10, x11
    assert step_word(PROG_MUL, 0, 9) == 0x937ffd48;
    assert step_word(PROG_MUL, 1, 9) == 0xca080129;
    assert step_word(PROG_MUL, 11, 9) == 0xeb1f015f;
    assert step_word(PROG_MUL, 12, 9) == 0xfa5f1184;
    assert step_word(PROG_MUL, 14, 9) == 0x9bcb7d50;
    // orr x16, x16, x17; mul x17, x9, x12; eor x10, x16, x8; ccmp x16, xzr, #0, ne
    assert step_word(PROG_MUL, 16, 9) == 0xaa110210;
    assert step_word(PROG_MUL, 20, 9) == 0x9b0c7d31;
    assert step_word(PROG_MUL, 27, 9) == 0xca08020a;
    assert step_word(PROG_MUL, 33, 9) == 0xfa5f1200;
    // and x8, x11, x12; mvn x8, x8; mov x16, #0x8000000000000000; mov x0, x9; mov x3, x12; mov x9, x0
    assert step_word(PROG_DIV, 3, 9) == 0x8a0c0168;
    assert step_word(PROG_DIV, 4, 9) == 0xaa2803e8;
    assert step_word(PROG_DIV, 5, 9) == 0xd2f00010;
    assert step_word(PROG_DIV, 11, 9) == 0xaa0903e0;
    assert step_word(PROG_DIV, 14, 9) == 0xaa0c03e3;
    assert step_word(PROG_DIV, 16, 9) == 0xaa0003e9;
    // mov x8, #128; cmp x11, x8; lsl x8, x10, x11; mvn x16, x11; lsr x17, x9, #1; lsr x16, x17, x16; lsl x16, x9, x11
    assert step_word(PROG_SHL, 0, 9) == 0xd2801008;
    assert step_word(PROG_SHL, 1, 9) == 0xeb08017f;
    assert step_word(PROG_SHL, 3, 9) == 0x9acb2148;
    assert step_word(PROG_SHL, 4, 9) == 0xaa2b03f0;
    assert step_word(PROG_SHL, 5, 9) == 0xd341fd31;
    assert step_word(PROG_SHL, 6, 9) == 0x9ad02630;
    assert step_word(PROG_SHL, 8, 9) == 0x9acb2130;
    // mov x17, #64; tst x11, x17; csel x10, x16, x8, ne; csel x9, xzr, x16, ne
    assert step_word(PROG_SHL, 9, 9) == 0xd2800811;
    assert step_word(PROG_SHL, 10, 9) == 0xea11017f;
    assert step_word(PROG_SHL, 11, 9) == 0x9a88120a;
    assert step_word(PROG_SHL, 12, 9) == 0x9a9013e9;
    assert step_word(PROG_SHL_W, 0, 9) == 0x9acb2148;
    // lsr x8, x9, x11; lsl x17, x10, #1; lsl x16, x17, x16; asr x16, x10, x11; csel x9, x16, x8, ne;
    // asr x17, x10, #63; csel x10, x17, x16, ne
    assert step_word(PROG_SHR, 3, 9) == 0x9acb2528;
    assert step_word(PROG_SHR, 5, 9) == 0xd37ff951;
    assert step_word(PROG_SHR, 6, 9) == 0x9ad02230;
    assert step_word(PROG_SHR, 8, 9) == 0x9acb2950;
    assert step_word(PROG_SHR, 11, 9) == 0x9a881209;
    assert step_word(PROG_SHR, 12, 9) == 0x937ffd51;
    assert step_word(PROG_SHR, 13, 9) == 0x9a90122a;
    // umulh x8, x9, x11; mul x16, x9, x12; adds x8, x8, x16; mul x16, x10, x11; adds x10, x8, x16; mul x9, x9, x11
    assert step_word(PROG_MUL_W, 0, 9) == 0x9bcb7d28;
    assert step_word(PROG_MUL_W, 1, 9) == 0x9b0c7d30;
    assert step_word(PROG_MUL_W, 2, 9) == 0xab100108;
    assert step_word(PROG_MUL_W, 3, 9) == 0x9b0b7d50;
    assert step_word(PROG_MUL_W, 4, 9) == 0xab10010a;
    assert step_word(PROG_MUL_W, 5, 9) == 0x9b0b7d29;
    // and x9, x9, x11; orr x10, x10, x12; eor x9, x9, x11; asr x8, x9, #63; cmp x10, x8; cmp x10, xzr; mov x0, x9
    assert step_word(PROG_AND, 0, 9) == 0x8a0b0129;
    assert step_word(PROG_OR, 1, 9) == 0xaa0c014a;
    assert step_word(PROG_XOR, 0, 9) == 0xca0b0129;
    assert step_word(PROG_CAST_S, 0, 9) == 0x937ffd28;
    assert step_word(PROG_CAST_S, 1, 9) == 0xeb08015f;
    assert step_word(PROG_CAST_U, 0, 9) == 0xeb1f015f;
    assert step_word(PROG_REM, 3, 9) == 0xaa0903e0;
}

// The model of each program against the reference's own i128 arithmetic, for every pair of samples: the same
// value when the exact result is an i128 (and the divisor is not 0, and not minInt / -1), else a trap at the
// site Zig's Debug build panics at.
test every_program_against_i128_arithmetic {
    var i : u32 = 0;
    var checked : u32 = 0;
    while (i < SAMPLES) {
        var j : u32 = 0;
        while (j < SAMPLES) {
            const al : u64 = sample_word(i, 0);
            const ah : u64 = sample_word(i, 1);
            const bl : u64 = sample_word(j, 0);
            const bh : u64 = sample_word(j, 1);
            const x : i128 = sample_value(i);
            const y : i128 = sample_value(j);
            const add : PairRun = run_steps(PROG_ADD, al, ah, bl, bh);
            if (sum_fits(i, j)) {
                assert add.trap == RUN_OK and t27b_i128_join(add.lo, add.hi) == x + y;
            } else {
                assert add.trap == 1;
            }
            const sub : PairRun = run_steps(PROG_SUB, al, ah, bl, bh);
            if (difference_fits(i, j)) {
                assert sub.trap == RUN_OK and t27b_i128_join(sub.lo, sub.hi) == x - y;
            } else {
                assert sub.trap == 1;
            }
            const mul : PairRun = run_steps(PROG_MUL, al, ah, bl, bh);
            if (product_fits(i, j)) {
                assert mul.trap == RUN_OK and t27b_i128_join(mul.lo, mul.hi) == x * y;
            } else {
                assert mul.trap == 1;
            }
            const div : PairRun = run_steps(PROG_DIV, al, ah, bl, bh);
            if (y == 0) {
                assert div.trap == 1;
            } else if (x == MIN128 and y == 0 - 1) {
                assert div.trap == 2;
            } else {
                assert div.trap == RUN_OK and t27b_i128_join(div.lo, div.hi) == @divTrunc(x, y);
            }
            // @rem traps only on a zero divisor: minInt % -1 is 0.
            const rem : PairRun = run_steps(PROG_REM, al, ah, bl, bh);
            if (y == 0) {
                assert rem.trap == 1;
            } else {
                assert rem.trap == RUN_OK and t27b_i128_join(rem.lo, rem.hi) == @rem(x, y);
            }
            // The wrapping and bitwise programs never trap.
            const add_w : PairRun = run_steps(PROG_ADD_W, al, ah, bl, bh);
            assert add_w.trap == RUN_OK and t27b_i128_join(add_w.lo, add_w.hi) == x +% y;
            const sub_w : PairRun = run_steps(PROG_SUB_W, al, ah, bl, bh);
            assert sub_w.trap == RUN_OK and t27b_i128_join(sub_w.lo, sub_w.hi) == x -% y;
            const mul_w : PairRun = run_steps(PROG_MUL_W, al, ah, bl, bh);
            assert mul_w.trap == RUN_OK and t27b_i128_join(mul_w.lo, mul_w.hi) == x *% y;
            const both : PairRun = run_steps(PROG_AND, al, ah, bl, bh);
            assert both.trap == RUN_OK and t27b_i128_join(both.lo, both.hi) == (x & y);
            const either : PairRun = run_steps(PROG_OR, al, ah, bl, bh);
            assert either.trap == RUN_OK and t27b_i128_join(either.lo, either.hi) == (x | y);
            const differ : PairRun = run_steps(PROG_XOR, al, ah, bl, bh);
            assert differ.trap == RUN_OK and t27b_i128_join(differ.lo, differ.hi) == (x ^ y);
            checked = checked + 1;
            j = j + 1;
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    assert checked == SAMPLES * SAMPLES;
}

/// How many shift amounts the shift test takes.
const AMOUNTS : u32 = 12;

/// Shift amount j: both sides of 64 and of 128, a u32's greatest, and a negative i64's word.
fn amount(j: u32) -> u64 {
    if (j == 0) { return 0; }
    if (j == 1) { return 1; }
    if (j == 2) { return 31; }
    if (j == 3) { return 63; }
    if (j == 4) { return 64; }
    if (j == 5) { return 65; }
    if (j == 6) { return 100; }
    if (j == 7) { return 127; }
    if (j == 8) { return 128; }
    if (j == 9) { return 129; }
    if (j == 10) { return 4294967295; }
    return MAX64;
}

// Each shift program against the reference's i128 shifts, for every sample and amount: a checked shift traps at
// its site from 128 up; a wrapping one shifts by the amount modulo 128.
test every_shift_against_i128_shifts {
    var i : u32 = 0;
    var checked : u32 = 0;
    while (i < SAMPLES) {
        var j : u32 = 0;
        while (j < AMOUNTS) {
            const al : u64 = sample_word(i, 0);
            const ah : u64 = sample_word(i, 1);
            const n : u64 = amount(j);
            const x : i128 = sample_value(i);
            const shl : PairRun = run_steps(PROG_SHL, al, ah, n, 0);
            const shr : PairRun = run_steps(PROG_SHR, al, ah, n, 0);
            if (n < 128) {
                const k : u32 = n as u32;
                assert shl.trap == RUN_OK and t27b_i128_join(shl.lo, shl.hi) == x << k;
                assert shr.trap == RUN_OK and t27b_i128_join(shr.lo, shr.hi) == x >> k;
            } else {
                assert shl.trap == 1 and shr.trap == 1;
            }
            const m : u32 = (n & 127) as u32;
            const shl_w : PairRun = run_steps(PROG_SHL_W, al, ah, n, 0);
            const shr_w : PairRun = run_steps(PROG_SHR_W, al, ah, n, 0);
            assert shl_w.trap == RUN_OK and t27b_i128_join(shl_w.lo, shl_w.hi) == x << m;
            assert shr_w.trap == RUN_OK and t27b_i128_join(shr_w.lo, shr_w.hi) == x >> m;
            checked = checked + 1;
            j = j + 1;
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    assert checked == SAMPLES * AMOUNTS;
}

// A checked cast to a narrower type traps when the high word is not the low word's extension; a truncating one
// never does. The low word's own check is codegen.rs's cast from u64 or i64.
test a_cast_checks_the_high_word {
    var i : u32 = 0;
    while (i < SAMPLES) {
        const lo : u64 = sample_word(i, 0);
        const hi : u64 = sample_word(i, 1);
        const x : i128 = sample_value(i);
        assert (run_steps(PROG_CAST_U, lo, hi, 0, 0).trap == 1) == (hi != 0);
        assert (run_steps(PROG_CAST_S, lo, hi, 0, 0).trap == 1) == (hi != asr_word(lo, 63));
        assert run_steps(PROG_TRUNC, lo, hi, 0, 0).trap == RUN_OK;
        assert (hi == 0) == (x >= 0 and x <= 18446744073709551615);
        assert (hi == asr_word(lo, 63)) == (x >= 0 - 9223372036854775808 and x <= 9223372036854775807);
        i = i + 1;
    }
}

test the_division_routine_takes_each_path {
    // Both fit 64 bits: one division of words.
    assert t27b_i128_div(7, 0, 2, 0) == 3;
    assert t27b_i128_div(MAX64, 0, 1, 0) == 18446744073709551615;
    // A divisor of 32 bits: the high word first, then two digits. 2^127 - 1 over 10, and over -16.
    assert t27b_i128_div(MAX64, SIGN64 - 1, 10, 0) == 17014118346046923173168730371588410572;
    assert t27b_i128_div(MAX64, SIGN64 - 1, MAX64 - 15, MAX64) == 0 - 10633823966279326983230456482242756607;
    assert t27b_i128_div(0, 1, LOW32, 0) == 4294967297;
    // A wider divisor: binary long division. 2^127 - 1 over 2^64, over 2^64 - 1, over 2^96 + 7.
    assert t27b_i128_div(MAX64, SIGN64 - 1, 0, 1) == 9223372036854775807;
    assert t27b_i128_div(MAX64, SIGN64 - 1, MAX64, 0) == 9223372036854775808;
    assert t27b_i128_div(MAX64, SIGN64 - 1, 7, LOW32 + 1) == 2147483647;
    assert t27b_i128_div(0, SIGN64, 7286977268806824, 0) == 0 - 23348663949973909715360;
    // The least i128 over 1 and over 2, and a negative quotient of each sign of operand.
    assert t27b_i128_div(0, SIGN64, 1, 0) == MIN128;
    assert t27b_i128_div(0, SIGN64, 2, 0) == 0 - 85070591730234615865843651857942052864;
    assert t27b_i128_div(MAX64 - 6, MAX64, 2, 0) == 0 - 3;
    assert t27b_i128_div(7, 0, MAX64 - 1, MAX64) == 0 - 3;
    assert t27b_i128_div(MAX64 - 6, MAX64, MAX64 - 1, MAX64) == 3;
    assert t27b_i128_div(3, 0, 7, 0) == 0;
    // The routine's names are the ones the splice renames, and DIV_ROUTINE is this one renamed.
    assert std.mem.indexOf(u8, HELPER, PORT) != null;
    assert std.mem.eql(u8, DIV_ROUTINE, "__t27b_i128_div");
    assert std.mem.eql(u8, REM_ROUTINE, "__t27b_i128_rem");
    assert std.mem.eql(u8, BUILTINS, "@divTrunc @rem");
}

test the_remainder_routine_takes_each_path_and_the_dividends_sign {
    // Both fit 64 bits; a divisor of 32 bits; a wider one.
    assert t27b_i128_rem(7, 0, 2, 0) == 1;
    assert t27b_i128_rem(MAX64, SIGN64 - 1, 10, 0) == 7;
    assert t27b_i128_rem(MAX64, SIGN64 - 1, MAX64, 0) == 9223372036854775807;
    assert t27b_i128_rem(MAX64, SIGN64 - 1, 0, 1) == 18446744073709551615;
    assert t27b_i128_rem(MAX64, SIGN64 - 1, 7, LOW32 + 1) == 79228162514264337578511564806;
    // The sign of the dividend: -7 % 2 is -1, 7 % -2 is 1, -7 % -2 is -1.
    assert t27b_i128_rem(MAX64 - 6, MAX64, 2, 0) == 0 - 1;
    assert t27b_i128_rem(7, 0, MAX64 - 1, MAX64) == 1;
    assert t27b_i128_rem(MAX64 - 6, MAX64, MAX64 - 1, MAX64) == 0 - 1;
    // minInt % -1 and minInt % 1 are 0; minInt % 3 is -2.
    assert t27b_i128_rem(0, SIGN64, MAX64, MAX64) == 0;
    assert t27b_i128_rem(0, SIGN64, 1, 0) == 0;
    assert t27b_i128_rem(0, SIGN64, 3, 0) == 0 - 2;
    assert t27b_i128_rem(3, 0, 7, 0) == 3;
}
